# IntervYou Architecture & Systems Design Reference

This document provides a detailed breakdown of the architectural decisions, trade-offs, distributed systems patterns, optimizations, and technologies implemented within the IntervYou collaborative interview platform.

---

## 1. Technology Stack Overview

| Component | Technology | Role & Benefit |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Core Framework** | Next.js (App Router, API Routes) | Provides server-side rendering (SSR), search engine optimization (SEO), and dynamic API route handling. |
| **Realtime Signaling** | Supabase WebSockets | Handles live messaging channels and presence coordination without hosting dedicated socket servers. |
| **Keystroke Sync** | Yjs CRDT + `y-webrtc` (P2P) + `y-monaco` | Coordinates conflict-free live document editing via Peer-to-Peer WebRTC, with a fail-safe fallback to Supabase Realtime. |
| **Media Engine** | LiveKit Cloud SFU + WebRTC Fallback (P2P + Google/Twilio STUN) | Powers optimized multi-stream video, audio, and screen-share using LiveKit Cloud, with an automatic fallback to P2P WebRTC using Google/Twilio STUN servers if LiveKit is offline. |
| **Collaborative Whiteboard** | Excalidraw + Supabase Realtime | Provides a shared sketching board with real-time canvas element sync over dedicated Supabase whiteboard channels. |
| **Database** | PostgreSQL + Prisma ORM | Stores persistent user data, session histories, configurations, and submission records. |
| **Caching Layer** | Redis (`ioredis`) | Holds ephemeral, high-frequency session backups to support fast restoration after dropouts. |
| **AI Orchestration** | Gemini API (2.5 Flash / Lite) | Generates dynamic problems, skeletons, dynamic test cases, and reflection drivers. |
| **Code Execution** | Piston API + Judge0 Fallback | Executes untrusted user code using Piston API with an automatic fallback to Judge0 sandboxes. |

