## 6. Submissions, History & Retrieval Optimizations

To handle high-scale data retrieval and prevent database or network bottlenecks, we implemented database indexing, selective query projection, and dynamic on-demand loading.

### A. Selective Query Projection & Payload Size Reduction
* **Problem:** Originally, fetching the list of 50 submissions via `GET /api/submissions` loaded the entire user-written `code` block (up to 10KB+ per file) and all detailed `testResults` (including stdout, error traces, and expected/actual outputs for all test cases). This resulted in multi-megabyte JSON payloads and heavy database serialization.
* **Solution:** Configured the listing API in [app/api/submissions/route.ts](file:///e:/Local/javascript/interv/app/api/submissions/route.ts) to use Prisma `select` projection:
  * Omit the large `code` text field from list queries.
  * Omit large test run diagnostics (stdout, expected/actual outputs, errors) from nested `testResults` queries, fetching only the lightweight `passed` boolean status.
* **Benefit:** Reduces list retrieval payloads by over 95%, speeding up network transit and JSON parsing times on the client.

### B. On-Demand Submission Details Loading
* **Approach:** To retain full detail viewing capabilities without the payload bloat:
  * Added a single-submission fetch endpoint: `GET /api/submissions?id=<submissionId>` which returns the complete record (full code and detailed test logs).
  * Updated client-side states in [app/dashboard/page.tsx](file:///e:/Local/javascript/interv/app/dashboard/page.tsx), [app/submissions/page.tsx](file:///e:/Local/javascript/interv/app/submissions/page.tsx), and [app/dashboard/submissions/page.tsx](file:///e:/Local/javascript/interv/app/dashboard/submissions/page.tsx) to lazy-load the submission code and detailed diagnostics on-demand only when a user triggers "Show Code" or clicks "View" details.

### C. Eliminate N+1 Secondary Notes Queries
* **Problem:** The system previously retrieved interviewer notes using a secondary, raw SQL query (`getInterviewerNotesForSessions`) catching dynamic errors for backward compatibility with older migrations. Running a second query for every list fetch added database roundtrip overhead.
* **Solution:** Now that migrations are finalized, `interviewerNotes` is fetched directly in the main `select` block of the primary queries in [app/api/submissions/route.ts](file:///e:/Local/javascript/interv/app/api/submissions/route.ts) and [app/api/history/route.ts](file:///e:/Local/javascript/interv/app/api/history/route.ts).
* **Benefit:** Eliminates secondary queries entirely, reducing history and submissions database roundtrips down to a single query execution.

### D. Targeted Database Indexes
* **Approach:** Added performance indexes to the PostgreSQL schema in [prisma/schema.prisma](file:///e:/Local/javascript/interv/prisma/schema.prisma) to cover the query filters and sort order:
  * `@@index([userId, updatedAt])` on `Submission`: Optimizes user submissions page list retrieval sorted by most recent first (`orderBy: { updatedAt: "desc" }`).
  * `@@index([createdBy, scheduledFor, createdAt])` and `@@index([inviteeEmail, scheduledFor, createdAt])` on `InterviewSession`: Prevents in-memory sorting or full-table scans for history/upcoming session lookups.

